    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43716" root="&#xA;                        من&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْ</span></b> 
                         [used for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا</span> in the sense of <i>What?</i> as in
the following of El-Khansà,
“
                            
                                <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلَا مَنْ لِعَيْنِى لَا تَجِفُّ دُمُوعُهَا</span>
                            <br />
                        ”
                        <i>O! what aileth mine eye, that its tears dry not?</i>
quoted in the TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فثأ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْ</span>: respecting
its dual <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنَانْ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنَيْنْ</span>, and its pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنُونْ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنِينْ</span>, see I'Ak, p. 319. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْ لِى بِكَذَا</span>: see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِ</span> (near the end of the paragraph).

